# Citation metadata for this repository (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# GitHub renders this as the "Cite this repository" panel.
#
# TODO after the Zenodo DOI is minted: uncomment the `identifiers:` block below
# and fill in the concept DOI.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the archived software release (via
  its Zenodo DOI) and the accompanying paper.
title: >-
  BNN-Robustness-Verification: code and data for "Robustness Verification of
  Binary Neural Networks: An Ising and Quantum-Inspired Framework"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end pipeline that maps the robustness verification of a binary
  neural network (BNN) to a Quadratic Constrained Boolean Optimization (QCBO)
  problem and then to a Quadratic Unconstrained Binary Optimization (QUBO)
  instance, so that the verification query can be attacked with conventional
  solvers as well as with Ising-style, annealing and quantum-inspired hardware.
  The repository contains the QUBO construction, BNN training and binarized
  dataset preparation, simulated-annealing, Free Energy Machine, Gurobi and
  Z3/SMT solvers, independent counterexample checking, a hidden-layer width
  scaling sweep with its trained checkpoints and stored solver records, and
  verify_paper.py, a single command that re-checks those entries of Tables II
  to VII of the paper, of its hidden-layer width-scaling table, and of the
  Section IV-B claims made in prose, that can be recomputed from the shipped
  files.
